        "message": "MANUAL BOLA/IDOR: the API accepts X-User-Id from the client and returns int(x_user_id) as the effective principal without validating a signed token. In app/crud.py, _must_own_account(user_id, from_id) trusts this principal, so a caller may supply another customer's user id and select that customer's from_account_id. The issue is identity spoofing that defeats object-level authorization; dynamic runtime exploit confirmation is blocked by unresolved imports in app/main.py and missing Dockerfile in the archive.",
